# TestFlight observability (agent checklist)

After **`bun run ios:testflight`** completes and ASC shows **VALID**, run:

```bash
bun run ios:check-tf-feedback
bun run ios:check-asc-builds
```

| Command | Source | What it covers |
|---------|--------|----------------|
| `ios:check-tf-feedback` | ASC API + Luciq | Screenshot comments, crash submissions, Luciq MCP hint |
| `ios:check-asc-feedback` | ASC only | Same ASC half without Luciq |
| `ios:check-luciq` | Luciq | SDK + MCP cred check (`status: mcp` or `ok`) |
| `luciq:sync-secrets` | Doppler | Copy `LUCIQ_OAUTH_TOKEN` from `servers-teamkeys/dev` to `purple-life/prd` |
| `luciq:install-mcp` | Local Cursor | Merge Luciq HTTP MCP into `~/.cursor/mcp.json` (restart Cursor) |

## Luciq tokens (Doppler)

| Secret | Project / config | Purpose |
|--------|------------------|---------|
| `LUCIQ_APP_TOKEN` | `purple-life` / `prd` | SDK on device (TestFlight `--dart-define`) |
| `LUCIQ_OAUTH_TOKEN` | `servers-teamkeys` / `dev` | **Source** MCP/API token |
| `LUCIQ_API_TOKEN` | `purple-life` / `prd` | **Runtime** copy from sync (same value as OAuth token) |
| `LUCIQ_ACCOUNT_EMAIL` | `purple-life` / `prd` | Luciq account (`pmt@eatos.com`) |

Dashboard project: **Flutter - Purple - Beta**.

**Note:** MCP OAuth token does **not** authenticate legacy REST (`dashboard-api.instabug.com`).
`ios:check-luciq` returns `status: "mcp"` when creds are synced; use **Luciq MCP** in Cursor for crash stacks.

## When testers report crashes

1. ASC `betaFeedbackCrashSubmissions` is often **empty** for screenshot-only reports.
2. Run `bun run luciq:sync-secrets` if `dashboardApiConfigured` is false.
3. Run `bun run luciq:install-mcp` (once per machine), restart Cursor, query **Flutter - Purple - Beta** via Luciq MCP (`list_crashes`, etc.).
4. Track open issue **`tf-crash-report`** in `docs/OPEN-ISSUES.md`.

## Alternatives (policy)

See `mem/observability/crash-reporting.md`. Luciq stays primary for TestFlight until
`tf-crash-report` is resolved or cost/policy triggers migration (Sentry, Crashlytics).
